 "why": "The periodic table extended to element 140 (non-relativistic first pass: 6s, 4f, 5d, 6p, a noble gas expected at 138), cached element by element; nuclear statistical equilibrium for 4D (where deep burning ends, element by element, on the trusted drops); and more random starts for Xater's crystal in cells of 2 and 3 molecules. And 60 PxGl₂ placements against the repulsive wall (k 200–259): all 81 of the first set were bound, so the fitted field had no repulsion to learn. And our OF₂'s liquid on its MP2-fitted field (Gibbs, 120–260 K), the check of the whole chain: OF₂ boils at 128 K, critical near 258 K.",
